          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.122,
            0.332,
            0.143
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Temperature"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.15,
            0.886,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": "During summer time you would have heard in the news that there is a ‘heat wave’. What do you think will be the temperature during the summer when you feel very hot? In the winter we have cooler or colder temperatures."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.242,
            0.885,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": "What has been the maximum temperature during the summer and the minimum temperature during the winter last year in your area? Find out."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.31,
            0.886,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": "When we measure temperature, we use Celsius as the unit of measure $( ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C } )$ . The thermometers below are showing $4 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C }$ and $1 5 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$ temperatures."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.385,
            0.353,
            0.407
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.416,
            0.638,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": "1. Do you know that there are some places in India where temperatures can go below $0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C } ?$ Find out the places in India where temperatures sometimes go below $0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathsf { C }$ What is common among these places? Why does it become colder there and not in other places?"
        },
        {
